@moguw/pi-openai-tools

Source integration of pi-openai-toolkit version 0.14.5 (source snapshot;
no .git metadata was provided, so no toolkit commit is asserted), and
code-yeongyu/pi-apply-patch version 0.1.2 at commit
8f0d8a6ec67599305c19c92de328178e97522e1e.

The toolkit's original MIT license (Copyright (c) 2026 lll9p) is preserved
in LICENSE. Its unmodified NOTICE is in licenses/pi-openai-toolkit/NOTICE,
including awoaCrim and contributors, Oh My Pi (Mario Zechner, Can Bölük,
Stencil Labs, Inc.), and Igor Warzocha attribution. Its historical Web Search
attribution is retained for provenance; that implementation is NOT included.

The apply-patch original MIT license (Copyright (c) 2026 Yeongyu Kim) and
NOTICE are preserved unmodified in licenses/pi-apply-patch/.

Local adaptations: separate npm/workspace metadata, four explicit entries,
operational config path pi-openai-tools, removal of hosted Web Search and
auto-mode configuration/code, a type-safe read of the unchanged Astra input
tail, and Node/Vitest regression tests. Persistent
toolkit protocol markers and checkpoint formats retain their upstream names.
